      <p>For overweight or obese individuals, losing 7% to 10% of overall body weight is the most effective way to reduce liver fat, resolve inflammation, and potentially reverse early-stage fibrosis. Weight loss must be gradual (about 0.5 to 1 kg per week), as rapid weight loss can worsen liver fat accumulation.</p>
      
