      <p>Adjusting what you eat is one of the most effective ways to manage symptoms. Some patients benefit from a temporary <strong>Low FODMAP diet</strong> under the guidance of a nutritionist. Increasing soluble fiber (like psyllium husk) can help patients with IBS-C, while reducing insoluble fiber (like raw bran) can help patients with IBS-D. Sticking to regular meal timings is also beneficial.</p>
      
