      <p><strong>Q2: Why is my GERD worse at night?</strong><br/>
      GERD worsens at night because when you lie down, gravity can no longer help keep stomach acid in your stomach. Additionally, saliva production (which helps neutralize acid) and swallowing decrease during sleep, allowing refluxed acid to remain in the esophagus longer.</p>
      
